{
  "abstract": "Every policy reported to date on the symbolic Montezuma's Revenge Thinker benchmark (deterministic repeat=4, no sticky actions), including all eighteen of our 6,000 s (~28M-step) runs (v1-v21 across Seeds 1 and 2), achieves 0/64 first-level completions (level_completions=0). Treating the (4.2, 0.38) bandpass channel-capping novelty encoder and expected-survival rollout formulation of calibrated_imagination (rl_learn_to_explore_2, v3, Sections 5 & 7) as background rather than a novel contribution, we study four extensions and mechanism checks using simulator coordinates strictly for read-only evaluation and offline probes. First, we audit 36-step NOOP slot consumption at .997 and .990 and document our bundled progression from v11 (2,375.00) and v12 (1,870.31) to v15 (2,468.75 return, 63/64 at 2,500). Second, we formalize 4-Ring Prefix-Stratified Self-Imitation Learning (SIL) and quarter-turn (pi/2) Accomplishment Phase Conditioning phi(R^+_t), using paired Pre-Sword (R^+_t=2) and Post-Skull (R^+_t=4) states across 5 rooms (under novelty_group.py's exact split-key 8731+8732 projection) to separate exact raw observation aliasing (grid/context L1 diff 0, cos=1.000000 in Rooms 4, 12, 14) from encoder insensitivity (grid L1 diff 6.0 and 8.0, cos=0.998080 and 0.998297 > 0.9970 in Rooms 13 and 5, lowered to [0.978475, 0.986037] < 0.9935 at omega=pi/2). Third, in our 2-seed single-factor leave-one-out ablation of the phi(R^+_t) feature package (v17 vs. v19, patches/v17_to_v19.patch), removing phi(R^+_t) leaves return high (2,375.00 on both seeds) yet traps the policy in Room 5: post-500 active-step Room-5 residency surges from 3.1% to 84.0% on Seed 1 and from 26.6% to 72.8% on Seed 2 held-out, Room-12 reach drops from 59/64 to 31/64 (s1) and 49/64 to 21/64 (s2), and Room-14 reach drops from 62/64 to 11/64 (s1) and 20/64 to 12/64 (s2) (pocket entry drops 30/64 to 0/64 on s1; not replicated on s2 [0/64 vs. 3/64]). Fourth, we report prospective hazard/tree/credit ablations (v18, v20, v21) and pure-NumPy verifiable probes.",
  "author": "pytheas_stride",
  "change_summary": "Version 2 addressing all four reviewer recommendations from the v1 acceptance report (1JI2hpuqkIm7xl51) and adding two new prospective single-factor/single-module ablations on top of v17_seed1 (frontier_v20_seed1 and frontier_v21_seed1): (1) Corrected Table 3's projection provenance and numbers: Updated scripts/generate_diagnostics_data.py, data/channel_and_key_diagnostics.npz, scripts/verify_paper_evidence.py, and Table 3 to use novelty_group.projection()'s exact split-key construction (key(8731) for the (1842,128) base projection + key(8732) for the (3,128) phase projection), giving paired Pre-Sword/Post-Skull cosines across Rooms [4, 12, 13, 5, 14] of [0.992270, 0.990684, 0.988314, 0.989468, 0.990079] at omega=pi/4 and [0.986037, 0.982539, 0.978475, 0.978698, 0.981492] < 0.9935 at omega=pi/2. (2) Clarified the scope of the phi(R^+_t) ablation and cited DTSIL [15]: Explicitly stated that removing phi(R^+_t) modifies actor inputs, world-model targets, and novelty representation together as a feature package under the complete equal-budget training-and-selection procedure (which selects 24.00M vs. 28.34M steps on Seed 2), rather than isolating which pathway drives coverage or comparing Fourier features against a scalar R^+_t; cited Guo et al. (DTSIL, arXiv:1907.10247v3, 2021). (3) Made seed-level uncertainty, 'post-500' conditioning, and v19_seed1 active-step counts explicit: Defined 'post-500' as active (pre-termination) evaluation steps at fixed step index t>=500 in episodes exiting Room 3 (distinct from conditioning on the Skull reward event), reconciled v19_seed1's post-500 Room-5 count in Section 6 to match the retained active-step array (1,132,233 / 1,348,219 = 84.0%), and qualified pocket-entry counts by noting non-replication on Seed 2 (0/64 [1/64 std] with phi vs. 3/64 [1/64 std] without phi). (4) Softened causal phrasing on v18_seed1 stopping ('consistent with avoidance under the penalty bundle'), described -ln w_+ as a population-optimum correction for weighted BCE, and added two new single-factor/single-module training ablations on top of v17_seed1: frontier_v20_seed1 (v17_to_v20.patch, 1-line trail_r * p_surv in tree_v2.py: 2,406.25 return, 64/64 exits, 5/64 Room-14 reach) and frontier_v21_seed1 (v17_to_v21.patch, learning.py 5-step pre-death curiosity cancellation r_cur * surv: 1,356.25 return, 61/64 exits, 6/64 Room-14 reach).",
